# Toronto Rising — dashboard SCSS nesting

Dashboard styles live in `.dev/storyteller-dashboard/src/client/styles/` as **SCSS only**. Vite compiles them (imported from the React entry). Do **not** add or edit a `src/client/styles.css` source file.

## Nest whenever possible

- Put descendants, pseudos, and state classes **inside** their parent block (`&:hover`, `&[hidden]`, `img`, `button`).
- For a block’s own BEM suffixes on the **same element or family**, use `&-seat`, `&-text`, `&-error` — not a second top-level `.scenes-token-seat { }`.
- Put `@media` **inside** the block it changes, not as a file-level dump of that block’s properties.
- Combined states nest under the block: `&.expanded`, `&.favorite`, `&.added.lock.active`.

## Do not flatten

```scss
// ❌ BAD — related selectors as siblings
.scenes-token { width: 2.4%; }
.scenes-token-bg { border-radius: 50%; }
.scenes-token img { pointer-events: none; }

// ✅ GOOD
.scenes-token {
  width: 2.4%;
  img,
  &-bg { pointer-events: none; }
  &-bg { border-radius: 50%; }
}
```

## Allowed as top-level (not nested)

- `:root`, `html` / `body`, universal reset (`*`)
- A **new** component block (` .scenes-panel`, `.modal-backdrop`) — then nest **everything belonging to that block**
- Selectors that are truly shared across unrelated blocks (`button` reset, `.status`, `.lock.active`) — nest their own variants (`&:hover`, `&.error`)

Do not nest unrelated components inside each other just to create nesting. Depth of 3–4 is normal; if a nest is deeper, split a partial (`_scenes.scss`, `_stage-npcs.scss`), still nested inside each partial.
